{
  "name": "arch_bridge",
  "version": 2,
  "introduced_by": "redrock",
  "notes": "The 1929 steel deck-arch bridge over Sorrel Canyon: 88 m long and 8.5 m wide along local X, twin lattice ribs springing from concrete skewbacks 20 m below the deck, braced columns carrying a concrete deck with a 6 m asphalt road, 1 m footways and 1.25 m open railings. Faces along X (road runs west-east); it carves nothing and base rim sets the deck on the canyon rims.",
